JAEASortIO input syntax

Time Units Note
    While the event building and TTree are in time stamp 10ns ticks,
    all user inputs, and detector classes, have been converted to ns for ease.

GENERAL INPUT METHODS
  options file:
    file.info
      Info files contain the same syntax as command-line input.
      Info files are expanded inline, and may themselves reference further info files.
      Lines beginning with hash (#) are treated as comments and ignored.

  numeric options:
    -OptionName value
      stores value under OptionName for later access via IO::TestInput() and IO::GetInput().
    -vec Name x y z
      stores an XYZ vector under Name for later access via IO::GetXYZVectorInput().

  particle-ID gates / Graph inputs:
    -ID GateFile.root gate_id
    -GR GraphFile.root gate_id
      loads the first TGraph inheriting object (inc TCutG) found in GateFile.root and associates it with gate_id.

DATA FILES INPUT / OUTPUT
  bin run input:
    -bin /filepath/runprefix
      Or provide one non-.root argument to use as the digitiser run stem.
      e.g. /Data/run_
  event tree output (from bin):
    -tree / -T
      Writes the event tree to /filepath/runprefix.root.
    -treepath /path/to/output
      Writes the event tree output to /path/to/output/runprefix.root.
  event tree input (to sort histograms):
    file.root
    '/path/run*.root'
      Note: If an event tree input includes file.root, 
      Matching split files file_1.root, file_2.root, ... are added automatically.
      Duplicate inputs are removed after wildcard expansion and split-file discovery.
  histogram output:
    -H / -h
      Build histograms with automated filename /filepath/runprefix_hist.root
    -hist path/hist.root
      Build histograms with manual path/filename
    NOTE: While options -tree and -h *can* be used together, due to reasons of root-file efficiency, it is about 30-50% faster to run the program sequentially. 
  overwrite:
    -O / -o
      Enables overwrite mode for event tree and histogram outputs.

EVENT BUILDING CONFIGURATION
  Digitiser module order;
    -APV8104 zeroindex
    -APV8032 zeroindex
    -APV8016A zeroindex
      zeroindex is the module number corresponding to fmodl=1.
      If not provided, modules are indexed automatically by .bin file discovery.
      If any runs are missing a data file i.e. not using all modules, auto discovery should NOT be used.
    -TriggerModule N
      Repeat for mutliple modules.
      When provided, only built events containing at least one hit from one of these module numbers are written.
      Only hits from these modules extend the build window after building a candidate event has started.
  Digitiser timestamp offsets:
    -TOffN offset
      Applies `offset` to every timestamp read from module `N`.
      Example: `-TOff4 400`
      Offsets may be negative. Given in ns
      Applied before event building. Use cal file for small individual channel adjustments
  Time Sorting:
    -Window ns
      Coincidence build window in ns for grouping hits into one built event.
    -BinChunk N
      Raw digitiser read chunk size used before local sorting.
      BinChunk <<< BuildBuffer    Recommended 1-100
    -Tolerance ns
      Timestamp ordering tolerance forwarded to the digitiser readers.
    -MaxTs ticks
      Optional, maximum timestamp for raw digitiser sorting (experimental).
      Given in raw timestamp ticks to match timestamp disorder messages. 
      When globalMaxTs surpasses this value, digitiser buffer filling stops and final events are drained normally.
      Use for indivdual runs in which data became unusable at some mid-point.

GENERAL HISTOGRAM SORTING
  -Workers N
    Number of histogram worker threads for tree->hist and chunk->hist stages.
  -BuildBuffer N
    Active event buffer size used by the built-event builder.
    Too small may give Time Errors due to digitiser disorder
    Default 1,000,000
  -HistChunks N
    Built-event count per histogram chunk in the direct bin->hist path.
  -BasicHistograms 0|1
    When set non-zero, only the detector-class-free basic histograms are created and filled.
  -HistogramTimers 0|1
    Debugging option for sort speed.
    When set non-zero, prints total FillHistogramsBasic time plus four FillHistograms chunk timers.


DETECTOR CLASSES

  calibration file:
    file.cal
  File containing the map of digitiser channel to detector class, 
  pol2 energy calibration parameters and per-channel time offsets.
  If command list include multiple .cal arguments the final one listed will be used.

  -vec CdTe x y z (mm)
    Applies one XYZ position offset vector to focal point
  -CdTeFace zy mm
    Over-ride the distance between CdTe face and CdTe focal point (Default 30)
  -CdTeAngle1/-CdTeAngle2/-CdTeAngle3/-CdTeAngle4 degrees
    Over-ride the angles of the CdTe Quads (Defaults -65/-35/35/65)

  -vec S3 x y z (mm)
    Applies one XYZ position offset vector to S3 detector.
    The Z component is ADDED to S3TargetDistance (so either use delta-Z here or do not use S3TargetDistance).

  -S3FrontBackEnergy value
    S3 front/back energy matching tolerance.
  -S3FrontBackOffset value
    S3 front/back energy offset.
  -S3FrontBackTime ns
    S3 front/back time matching tolerance.
  -S3PreferenceSector 0|1
    Prefer sector energy when building S3 pixels.
  -S3MultiHit 0|1
    Allow S3 multi-hit pixel building.
  -S3KeepShared 0|1
    Keep S3 pixels that share ring or sector hits.
  -S3FlipPhi 0|1
    Flip the S3 phi convention. i.e. Change which way the detector is facing
  -S3TargetDistance distance (mm)
    S3 target distance used for hit positions. Can be negative for Upstream
  -S3OffsetPhiSetDeg degrees
    S3 phi offset in degrees. Angle between the signal cable and Phi=0

HISTOGRAM SORT SPECIFIC OPTIONS
Options only used in FillHistograms
i.e. not fundamental to event parsing of detector calses 

  Kinematics
    -BeamEnergy MeV
      Beam energy at mean interaction point.
      Used for generated kinematics and beta splines. Default 120.
    -BeamMass MeV/c^2
      Beam mass.
    -TargetMass MeV/c^2
      Target mass.
    -TargetLoss MeV
      Energy loss in MeV for target ion exiting target at from mean interaction position along Theta=0
      Angular correction assumes simple a 1/cos(theta) scaling.
    -BeamLoss MeV
      Energy loss in MeV for beam ion exiting target at from mean interaction position along Theta=180
    -GammaOffset distance (ns)
      Average time, in ns, before in-flight decay of target ion.
      Assuming a mean flight path along calculated target ion path before gamma decay.
    -BlurVectors
      Use blurred detector hit positions when calculating vectors.
    -PixelCutE energy
      Minimum S3 pixel energy used to selected "good" events.
      i.e. scatterd beam not light particles. Default 5.

  Coincidence Time Gates
    -CdTeS3Up ns
      CdTe-S3 upper prompt time gate. Default 100 ns.
    -CdTeS3Down ns
      CdTe-S3 lower prompt time gate. Default -100 ns.
    -CdTeS3BackUp ns
      CdTe-S3 upper background time gate. Default CdTeS3Up + 1500 ns.
    -CdTeS3BackDown ns
      CdTe-S3 lower background time gate. Default CdTeS3Down + 1500 ns.
    -HpGeS3Up ns
      HPGe-S3 upper prompt time gate. Default 100 ns.
    -HpGeS3Down ns
      HPGe-S3 lower prompt time gate. Default -100 ns.
    -HPGeS3BackUp ns
      HPGe-S3 upper background time gate. Default HpGeS3Up + 1500 ns.
    -HPGeS3BackDown ns
      HPGe-S3 lower background time gate. Default HPGeS3Down + 1500 ns.
    -CdTeCdTeGate ns
      CdTe-CdTe gamma-gamma prompt time gate. Default 100 ns.
    -CdTeHPGeUp ns
      CdTe-HPGe gamma-gamma upper time gate. Default 100 ns.
    -CdTeHPGeDown ns
      CdTe-HPGe gamma-gamma lower time gate. Default -100 ns.
    -HPGeHPGeGate ns
      HPGe-HPGe gamma-gamma prompt time gate. Default 100 ns.

  CdTe Time-Walk Correction (experimental)
    -CdTeS3TZero ns
      CdTe-S3 timing zero used for CdTe time-energy correction. Default 0 ns.
    -CdTeKeVns value
      CdTe time-energy correction slope. Default -1.
    -CdTeEZero keV
      CdTe time-energy correction reference energy. Default 120 keV.
